2 CONT
2 CONT The Treves family is known for its descent from''' Rashi,''' although the exact lineage, generation for generation, has not been preserved.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first to report this connection to the Luria - Spira family with the Treves family was R. Joseph Kohen-Zedek in "Dor Yesharim", published in HaGoren, Berdichev, 1898.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kohen-Zedek states that, regarding the lineage, he had received the information by oral tradition, "so I received it from my father.".  He was told that Solomon Spira's father was Samuel Spira, a brother-in-law of '''Jochanan Trev
2 CONC es'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is important to note that both Samuel Spira an Jochanan Treves are mentioned in the responsa of '''R. Joseph Colon.'''  Colon wrote, "Two great scholars of the past generation were the wonderous R. Johanan Treves an [his uncle]
2 CONC  R. Samuel Spira, of blessed memory."
2 CONT
2 CONT The sequence of generations and the fact that Jochanan Lurie of Alsace, son of Miriam, could have been named after her great-uncle, Jochanan son of R. Mattithiah Treves, lends support to this connection between the Luria-Spira and
2 CONC  Treves families.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note, that the '''Bodleian Library manuscript, #2240''' was based on Jochanan Luria's aancestry back to Rashi via the Spira lineage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Further, R. Solomon Lurie, the great Lublin scholar, known as the '''MaHaRaSHal''', wrote in his "Yam Shel Shlomo, Yebamot, 84, #33, "and I rely on the elaination of Rashi, from who stems the pedigree of my fther's house."
2 CONT
2 CONT . . . . .
2 CONT
2 CONT An article entitle  '''"From the Seed of Rashi"''' was published by Dr. Haim Chone in the scholarly journal "Sinai".  His introductory remarks refer to the earliest Treves source being "Birkat Avraam, published in 1524 and to the 
2 CONC 1575 responsa of the MaHaRaSHaL for the Lurie family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Next he discusses the '''origin of the Treves family name.''' The town associated with Rashi, '''Troyes''', was different at various historical periods.
2 CONT
2 CONT * The 11th-century '''French called it "Troies": '''
2 CONT * The''' Italians called it "Treci"'''
2 CONT *''' Rashi''' was known as '''Salomo Trecensis.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Chone presents a tree which he states is "as much as it appears to me to be the closest to the truth from sources."
2 CONT
2 CONT Chone presents the reader with a construction of what he thinks is the most likely genealogy of the Treves line.  the tree starts with one Moses, a student of '''Rashi,''' the father of '''Mattithiah the Great of Paris,''' father 
2 CONC of Jehiel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jehiel Treves of Paris was called "my relative" by Rashi's grandsons, R' Samuel ben Meir (died about 1174), known as RaSHBaM, and his brother, R. Jacob ben Meir (died in 1171 in Troyes), known as '''Rabeinu TaM,''' during their li
2 CONC fetime.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''The Lurie Legacy, by Neil Rosenstein Chapter 1 - Origins of the Lurie Family, Page 11''
2 CONT
2 CONT * See complete entry of Pages 11-12 in documents section.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Yosef Treves נולד: 1355 מקום: France נפטר: 1435 (בגיל ‎~80‏) מקום: Sicily, Italy Yosef Treves נולד: 1355 מקום: France נפטר: 1435 (בגיל ‎~80‏) מקום: Sicily, Italy
2 CONT
2 CONT הולדת הבן: Jehiel Treves הולדת הבן: Jochanan Treves הולדת הבן: Shmuel ben Joseph Treves Alsace, France 1435 גיל 79-80 פטירה Sicily, Italy 1435 1435 קבורה Sicily, Italy 1435 הולדת הבן: Jehiel Treves הולדת הבן: Jochanan Treves הולדת
2 CONC  הבן: Shmuel ben Joseph Treves Alsace, France 1435 גיל 79-80 פטירה Sicily, Italy 1435 1435 קבורה Sicily, Italy 1435
