1 NAME Süsskind (Schneur) /zum Stern/
2 GIVN Süsskind (Schneur)
2 _MARNM zum Stern
2 NICK Schneur ben Josef Jaakow
2 NICK Süsskind Kann
2 NICK Schneur
1 NAME סוסקין שנאור /שטרן/
2 GIVN סוסקין שנאור
2 SURN שטרן
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1610
2 PLAC Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preussen
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE 25 NOV 1686
2 PLAC Battonnstraße Jewish cemetery, Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preussen
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 NOV 1686
2 PLAC Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preussen
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} another possible death year is 1687
2 CONT
2 CONT Süsskind Stern was descended from one of the richest and most powerful 17th century families in the Judengasse. He was the founder of the Stern branch of the family, whilst his brother Isaak zur Kann founded the Kann branch. He to
2 CONC ok his family name from the family house at the sign of the Bunte Kanne, originally called Stern. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Stern dealt in jewellery and was a moneychanger, and in 1660 was listed as one of the most highlytaxed individuals in the Jewish community. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His sons, Isaac Süsskind and Samuel Stern, took over the family business on his death and continued to run it as partners. They also provided commissary services to the emperor's troops, supplying flour etc. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://www.judengasse.de/ehtml/P032.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT " Die Inschriften des Alten Judenfriedhofes in Wien " 
2 CONT
2 CONT Band II-by Dr. Bernhard Wachstein- pg. 24,25
