1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Menk's A Dictionary of German Jewish Surnames:
2 CONT
2 CONT Loans; Loanz 1) Etymology: T: from <Louans, Indre-et-Loire, France>. {cf. Elsässer (Worms); Michelstadt (Fürth); Wormser (Fulda; Michelstädter)}. - 2) Before 1800: R. Gershon Loans (d. 1484), after the expulsion from Louans in End
2 CONC ingen, Aargau, Switzerland, since 1478 in the Alsace; his son, R. Josef ben Gerson Loans (c.1478–1554), the famous “Josel von Rosheim”, 1484 in Haguenau, Bas-Rhin, France, 1500–14 in Mittelbergheim, Bas-Rhin, France, sc. 1514 in R
2 CONC osheim, Bas- Rhin, France; R. Josel's grandson, R. Eliyah ben Moshe Loans (1564–1636), born in Frankfurt am Main, F, Rabbi in Fulda, Hanau, Friedberg in Hessen, since ca. 1600 in Worms384; their descendants Loans or Loanz a.k.a. E
2 CONC lsass 1600–1710 Worms, WO; 1665 Mainz, MZ from Frankfurt am Main
2 CONT
2 CONT Loanz cf. Loans
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT peut-être né vers 1445
2 CONT
2 CONT lors de l'expulsion des Juifs d'Endingen, dans l'Etat de Bade, la famille Loans s'installe à Obernai, puis à Haguenau en 1476
2 CONT
2 CONT père inconnu
2 CONT
