1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The question of who is the father of R' Yekhiel Mikhel Spira is for the moment resolved. Until today there was was some uncertainty, but based on the longstanding work of several researchers studying this matter, i
2 CONC t appears that there is no such gravestone and therefore the best evidence currently available is the letter written in 1734 by Shmuel Porges, great grandson of R' Yekhiel Mikhel, who asserts in no uncertain terms that R' Yekhiel'
2 CONC s father was the 'Gaon' Shimon. If that aforementioned gravestone does appear one day, then the pedigree is easily correctable. (09 SEP 2024)
2 CONT
2 CONT For those wanting to review the various sources: 1) Jacobi Papers, Vol. 4, p. 189, 16.2 and p. 188, 15.2, asserting that there is a gravestone belonging to R' Yekhiel Mikhel Spira bearing an inscription naming Nathan as the father
2 CONC , 2) Lazarus, citing and fully inserting a letter written by Shmuel Porges in 1734 (a great grandson of R' Yekhiel Mikhel Spira), asserting that the father of R' Yekhiel Mikhel Spira was named Shimon: https://www.geni.com/document
2 CONC s/view?doc_id=6000000120835939887), and 3) Otser HaRabanim: # 9202, giving no father. (09 SEP 2024) 
