1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Die Familie Wolf" - by Ernst Wolf 1924 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.fpe.ch/stammbaum/ see pg. 118 
2 CONT
2 CONT see also chart Lion Gomperz &Lob Oppenheimer
2 CONT
2 CONT See also the Media tab of this profile for the document 'Descendancy Chart Spanier Nathan'.  Note: only the first 50 pages are viewable on screen.  The full 579 page document can be downloaded by clicking on 'Original PDF' on the 
2 CONC document page http://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000027396329758 which is accessible through the Media tab of this profile.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Spaniers" d'Irene Newhouse pour les mariages de Nathan Spanier :
2 CONT
2 CONT ..."Nathan owned his own house in Stadthagen, Krumme Strasse 35. He married Zippora, the daughter of a businessman in Stadthagen in 1598. A year later she bore him a daughter called Freude. Five other children followed: Isaak, Mos
2 CONC che, Chajim, Abraham and Esther but none of them had such a glittering marriage as the first born, 'our little Freude', of whom we shall learn more later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Whether all the children whose names have been passed down to us came from Zippora is not known, she died on 5th April 1632 and Nathan, as is expected of devout Jews, soon remarried - a girl by the name of Reize, daughter of Isaak
2 CONC . But she too had died by 1640, probably a victim of the then prevalent pest epidemic. and so it came that Nathan married a third time, this time with Hadassa, the daughter of Schmuel from Hildesheim"...
2 CONT
2 CONT See here information from Jüdischer Friedhof in Altona: http://www.steinheim-institut.de/cgi-bin/epidat?function=Ins&sel=hha&inv=3350
2 CONT
2 CONT The inscription reads:- ‎‏[פה נטמן היקר נתן]‏‎
2 CONT
2 CONT ‎‏[בר משה שפניר]‏‎	
2 CONT
2 CONT ‎‏[פרנס ומנהג דמדינת]‏‎
2 CONT
2 CONT ‎‏שומבורג מעשיו רק‏‎
2 CONT
2 CONT ‎‏תמימים [...] עולמו‏‎
2 CONT
2 CONT ‎‏יום ב׳ ד׳ כסליו [(ת״ז)]‏‎
2 CONT
2 CONT ‎‏לפ״ק תנצב״ה‏‎
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation:- Here is buried the dear Natan, Son of Moshe Spanier, President and Leader of the Provincial Jewish community of Schaumburg, his actions were only Perfect ... his world Monday, 4. Kislev.[12.11.1646]  of the small cou
2 CONC nt. May his soul be bound up in the bond of life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Commentary: Date: Died Monday, 12.11.1646 Natan Spanier was the "head of Schaumburg province" and the one who obtained the right to settle in Altona. He was based in Stadthagen, the then Count’s residence city of Holstein-Schaumbu
2 CONC rg. Freudchen, one of his two daughters, married Josef Hameln, the future father-in-law of Glückel of Hameln. The second daughter, Ester (No. -2492), was married to Löb Hildesheim. Of his four sons, Jizchak (no 2433) and Löb (no-3
2 CONC 325) are buried in Altona. The inscription is noticeably weathered, and it was so already at the beginning of the 20th century, because Duckesz printed it with many gaps in his 1915 published work. Row 4: From Feilchenfeld, Glücke
2 CONC l, it is known that Natan Spanier was "head of the Province of Schaumburg". Row 6: Year of death added according to Duckesz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants of Moses Spanier - page 1
2 CONT
2 CONT https://docslib.org/doc/2356440/descendants-of-nathan-spanier-17-feb-2014-page-1-1
2 CONT
