1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abraham_ben_Joseph_of_Orleans Abraham ben Joseph of Orleans] Wikipedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rabbi Abraham ben Joseph of Orleans''' (Hebrew: רבי אברהם בן יוסף; c. 1140) was an early 12th-century French Tosafist. Some have suggested that he is identical with Abraham ben Rabbi Joce (the Chief Rabbi of London in 1186). Ma
2 CONC ny of his interpretations of the Talmud are quoted several times in the Tosafot. Rabbi Abraham was born in Orléans, France in about 1140. His father, Joseph ben Isaac Bekhor Shor, was a famous Tosafist and a leading member of the 
2 CONC Orleans Jewish community. In his early years, Rabbi Abraham occupied a similar position. It was also during this time that he became acquainted with Rabbeinu Tam. Sometime after his daughter married Judah ben Isaac Messer Leon, Ra
2 CONC bbi Abraham may have moved to London where he served as Chief Rabbi in 1186
2 CONT
2 CONT
