2 CONT From the JewishEncyclopedia.com (1906):
2 CONT
2 CONT MANOAH B. JACOB    [is this a different person?]
2 CONT
2 CONT By: Isidore Singer, S. Kahn
2 CONT
2 CONT French Talmudist; lived at Lunel in the second half of the thirteenth century. He is sometimes quoted under the abbreviation  (="R. Manoah"; Halberstam MSS., No. 345).
2 CONT
2 CONT Manoah often cites decisions in the name of his father. After a brief residence at Narbonne, where he studied with Meïr b. Simon and Reuben b. Ḥayyim, Manoah returned to Lunel. Like several of his contemporaries, he was a student 
2 CONC of the works of Maimonides, and wrote a commentary on the latter's Yad ha-Ḥazaḳah, which is quoted in "Sha'are Ẓiyyon" under the title "Sefer ha-Manoaḥ," and in "Ḳore ha-Dorot," under the title "Sefer ha-Menuḥah." It was printed a
2 CONC t Constantinople in 1518.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography: Azulai, Shem ha-Gedolim, p. 60a; Conforte, Ḳore ha-Dorot, p. 17a; Isaac de Lattes, Sha'are Ẓiyyon, p. 75; Renan-Neubauer, Les Rabbins Français, p. 512; Fürst, Bibl. Jud.; Gross, Gallia Judaica, p. 285.
