1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Father of the Maharik, Solomon Trabotto was a noted Talmudist and Kabbalist, a scion of the Trabotto family, which was known for its large number of scholars. After the final expulsion of Jews from the French Kingd
2 CONC om in 1394, his family emigrated first to the Franche-Comté and subsequently settled in the city of Chambéry, the capital of the Duchy of Savoy, which was home to a significant population of rabbinic scholars. Among these were Yoh
2 CONC anan Treves, the last chief rabbi of France and Jacob HaLevi, renowned as Maharil Jacob ben Moses Möln.
2 CONT
