1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Katzenellenbogen family derive from the locality of Katzenelnbogen in the Prussian province of Hesse-Nassau. In 1312 Count Diether of Katzenelnbogen received permission from Emperor Henry VII. to keep twelve Je
2 CONC ws at Katzenelnbogen and Ludwig the Bavarian in 1330 permitted Count Wilhelm and his heirs to keep twenty-four Jews in their dominions (Böhmer, "Regesten," No. 501; Wiener, "Regesten," pp. 23, 33). Moshe Katzenelnbogen must have b
2 CONC een one of these and when he migrated to Italy was known as Moshe from Katzenelbogen
