1 OCCU Syndic des Juifs de Metz, rabbin ou "haver"
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} nommé TRENEL car natif de Tragny, entre Metz et Marsal? (Faustini) : les TRENEL et les GROTWOHL de Metz formeraient une seule famille, descendant des GROTWOHL de Francfort
2 CONT
2 CONT Metz Memorbuch #259 (folio 21a) [English Translation]: "The wise and humble trustee Samuel, son of Solomon, for he was a faithful shepherd for some years, and repeatedly left his home to go to places dangerous to the business of t
2 CONC he community. He attended the synagogue morning and evening and studied the Law regularly. He traded faithfully, was a skillful scribe and wrote a scroll of the Law for himself. His wife gave to charity for him." Died on Saturday 
2 CONC evening and buried on Sunday 8 Tammuz 5426 [11 Jul 1666]
2 CONT
2 CONT né vers 1605?
2 CONT
2 CONT réside à Metz après 1623/1624, date de son mariage avec la fille d'Isaac WALLICH
2 CONT
2 CONT Faustini p. 459
2 CONT
2 CONT voirTrenel de Metz p. 697 PAM
