1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Memorbuch #859 [English Translation]: "The eminent and pious Tsertche, daughter of Rabbi Isaac Jacob Trenel, who always conducted herself in justice and piety, mortified herself, forbade herself the superfluous, de
2 CONC spised the pleasures of this world... she took care to bring up her sons for study, honored the Law and those who study it, was generous to the poor... bequeathed a capital of 3,000 pounds, the income of which is to be used to clo
2 CONC the poor orphans every year, and another fund of 1,200 pounds, the income of which is to be used to feed the poor and poor women who give birth on Shabbat. She was a member of several pious women's brotherhoods to perform the last
2 CONC  duty. She spun Tsitsit... She was famous for her piety... Her sons donated to the hospice for her". She died on Tuesday and was buried on Wednesday, 13 Adar 5484 [8 Mar 1724]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Tsertché fille du rabbin Isaac Jacob Trenel "... voir Faustini p. 286
