1 NOTE {geni:about_me} And only one further clue is that the Moses who is father of this Herz Wetzlar https://www.geni.com/people/Herz-Wetzlar-zu-Offenbach/6000000044287075212  is very likely to be the one in the Offenbach Memorbuch: #28
2 CONC 9  Parnas Moshe Wetzlar, died in Iyar 1756, bn Josel Wetzlar.  If the Memorbuch can be used as a basis, Moshe is the only person surnamed Wetzlar who was living in Offenbach at the time of Karl Abraham's birth. However, if Moshe a
2 CONC nd Loeb are both sons of Josel, Loeb may have lived for awhile in Offenbach, too. But there is still a long way to go before we can say anything is actually proven, unfortunately.
