3 CITY Cracow
3 STAE Lesser Poland
3 CTRY Poland
1 OCCU Rav in Craow, avdak Levov
1 TITL R'
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rabbi Aharon the Darshan (Hakadosh) wrote the books: Bigdai Aharon, Mateh Aharon and Hoshen Aharon. He was murdered on his way to the Vaad Arbah Arazot.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/23996
2 CONT
2 CONT Die Inschriften des alten Judenfriedhofes in Wien by dr. Bernhard Wachstein- I Teil -page 416, 104, 192, 285,449 note 1,
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Aaron Teomim Frankel (son of Moshe Teomim Frankel) died 1690. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Aaron Teomim Frankel are: 
2 CONT *unknown* Teomim Frankel, b. 1690. http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/r/u/b/Leon-Rubinstein/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0462.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Wealthy and prominent family that produced rabbis and community leaders in Bohemia, Poland, and Galicia from the end of the sixteenth century. Mosheh Aharon Te’omim of Prague (d. 1609?) was the first to bear the family name. His d
2 CONC escendant, Aharon Te’omim (d. 1690), who wrote Mateh Aharon (1678), a commentary on the Haggadah, and Bigde Aharon (1710), a collection of homilies, was a preacher in Prague and a rabbi in Worms. In 1690 he began serving as rabbi 
2 CONC in Kraków, but several months later, while on his way to a meeting of the Council of Four Lands, he was arrested on the orders of a Polish nobleman, and died soon thereafter.  http://www.yivoencyclopedia.org/article.aspx/Teomim_Fa
2 CONC mily
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From "Tiferes Aryeh"
2 CONT
2 CONT Was Darshan and AB"D in Worms
2 CONT
2 CONT In the end of his days he was AB"D Krakow
2 CONT
2 CONT Killed in the city Chmielnick and brought to burial in Pintchov the city which is brother in law R. Leib I is buried.
