1 NAME Simon Joseph Isaac /Cahen/
2 GIVN Simon Joseph Isaac
2 _MARNM Cahen
2 NICK Shimon Cahen
2 NICK Ha Cohen
1 SEX M
1 OCCU unknown
2 PLAC Rabbin: Shimeon ben moreinu harav yosef itzah ha cohen
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1640
2 ADDR
3 CITY Frankfurt am Main
3 STAE Hesse
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 JUN 1713
2 ADDR
3 CITY Metz
3 STAE Lorraine
3 CTRY France
1 OCCU rabbin
1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Memorbuch #730 [English Translation]: The ancient, pious, upright, worthy, faithful, beneficent and illustrious Rabbi Simon, son of Rabbi Joseph Isaac Cahen of Frankfurt, who advanced in humility before God and men
2 CONC ..., did good..., did not allow himself to be brought down by suffering..., mortified himself for a long time by fasting and hardships... trained many pupils. He was a member of the brotherhood of those who study the Law and visit
2 CONC  the poor. He traded faithfully. His sons donated to charity for him". He died and was buried on Wednesday 13 Sivan 5473 [7 Jun 1713].
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon appears in an act of 09.05.1672 (act 788) with Bernard ZAY and Alexandre CAHEN his brother-in-law; we think that he married Anne, a daughter of Bernard ZAY (deceased in 1671, who thus transmits his first names Berman Issacha
2 CONC r to Simon's son). In 1694 (notice n° 517), Simon loses this still young son that we have just named (Berman Issachar), married in Poland and rabbi in Brest-Litovsk. In 1708, he signed the marriage contract of his daughter Genende
2 CONC lé (Kenendelet) as "son of Joseph Jacob Ha-Cohen" (3E 4105). [Faustini 290]
2 CONT
2 CONT Shimeon ben moreinu harav yosef itzah ha cohen
2 CONT
2 CONT "fils de Joseph Jacob Ha-Cohen" (Faustini p. 290)
